#### 3. Read-After-Write Conflicts (Phantom Reads)
**Vulnerability Type:** Read-After-Write Conflicts (Phantom Reads)  
**Severity:** Low  
**Affected Code Location:** `getMessage` function (line 60)  
**Description:** The `getMessage` function does not handle concurrent access to the same message. If multiple users are trying to read the same message at the same time, it could lead to phantom reads, where a user reads a message that has not been committed yet.  
**Recommended Fix:** Use a locking mechanism to ensure that only one user can read the message at a time. This can be done by using a mutex or a distributed lock.

```go
import (
	"sync"
)

var messageLocks = make(map[string]*sync.Mutex)

func (s *SmartContract) getMessage(APIstub shim.ChaincodeStubInterface, args []string) sc.Response {
